# Git-Based Production Deployment

The production server (68.183.168.75) has a git repo at `/opt/clinical-sovereignty-lab` tracking `origin/main` via HTTPS.

## Deployment Command

```bash
ssh root@68.183.168.75 "cd /opt/clinical-sovereignty-lab && git pull origin main && docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d --build"
```

## Rules

1. **Always use `docker compose` (space), not `docker-compose` (hyphen).**
2. **Always include `-f docker-compose.prod.yml`** — bare `docker compose up` uses the dev compose file with wrong volume mounts.
3. **Commit and push locally before pulling on production.** The server pulls from GitHub, not from the local machine.
4. **The remote uses HTTPS** (`https://github.com/Thera-cloud/Clinical-Sovereignty-Lab.git`), not SSH. No deploy key needed.
5. **Never run `git reset --hard` on production** without explicit approval — it discards server-local files (`.env`, data dirs).
6. **After every pull + rebuild, run the full post-deploy verification** per `build-deploy-ux-verification.mdc`: containers healthy, 112/112 services, bridge PG connected, ENVIRONMENT match.

## Workflow

1. Make changes locally (BLUE node)
2. `git add && git commit && git push origin main`
3. SSH to production and run the deployment command above
4. Verify health (see `build-deploy-ux-verification.mdc`)
